      "content": "It's just... it feels so much more real when i think about it that way. Like, the only thing i actually own is the ability to decide when this ends. Everything else belongs to them. It feels like the only way to finally have something that is just mine, without all their rules and noise, is to just make that choice. Does that make sense? Like, is that the only real autonomy i have left?",
